  "caveats": [
    "Even exclusively C-linked two-digit groups derive from an unverified community transcription of the official BLS XLS; counts reflect code correspondence, NOT proven Portuguese occupation classification.",
    "Mixed groups cover a large share of employment. No employment distribution within their four-digit units is observed in this dataset, so a precise C/N split is not identified.",
    "Provisional C-only and C+mixed fractions are NOT formally identified lower/upper bounds and must not be plugged into Fixed.cog_share.",
    "Eurostat OC63 is null/suppressed; don't impute, including zero; all-employed vs civilian frames differ and reliability flags apply.",
    "The 2024 public Eurostat two-digit dataset provides the SAME national employed population denominator as 2024 one-digit statistics, resolving the previous need to mix employer-only QP weights, but does not resolve 3/4-digit mixed codes.",
    "Original BLS binary workbook validation and mapped occupation-weighting remain scientific blockers. No Portugal model runs permitted.",
    "1,125 code pairs and titles match a separate BLS-branded XLS copy, but direct official BLS-hosted bytes remain unverified. Even at ISCO four-digit resolution, 26 codes have both C and N mappings."
  ]
}
